From 496d6a7713932224e1fd0d68c79d33dc80c57f41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 21:28:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] smart connect: explain the "- -" columns, and close an
 unclosed <td>

Investigating a report that a band showed "- -" for every field. It is not a
bug: on the reporting box smart_connect_selif_x=10 = SMRTCONN_SEL_5G |
SMRTCONN_SEL_6G, so 2.4 GHz is deliberately outside the Smart Connect group,
and smart_connect_x=2 is correctly derived from that mask. A simulator built
from the real bandName / get_wl_unit_by_band / wl_nband_title /
isSmartConnectSelifBand reproduces the screen exactly, and shows that labels
and cells agree in every dual/tri/quad configuration - so the suspected
header-versus-cell mismatch is refuted.

What was genuinely wrong is that "- -" explained nothing, which is why it read
as broken. All 13 suppressed-cell sites now route through one scExcludedCell()
helper carrying a hover title, and a note above the tables - shown only when a
column is actually suppressed - says the band is not in the Smart Connect
group, that its policy is not lost, where to change the selection, and that
6 GHz is excluded by default on this model.

That refactor also fixes a real markup defect: genSteerLoadBalance() opened a
<td>, wrote "- -" and then continued, skipping the code += '</td>' at the foot
of the loop, so the cell was never closed and later cells nested inside it.

Recorded for later: the wireless page's mask builder has a return 7 fallback,
and on a 2.4/5/6 box 7 means 2G + 5G + 5G2 - a radio that does not exist -
silently dropping 6 GHz. It is unreachable today, guarded by smartConnectEnable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp | 74 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 59 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp b/release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp
index da288ab398..d4fe47ac93 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp
@@ -130,6 +130,7 @@ let phyRate = [1148, 4804, 4804, 4804];
 function initial(){
 	show_menu();
 	setupSmartConnectToggle();
